*1) da'o is moved to selma'o UI. DAhO is almost UI anyway. *



*3) da'inai means this: the variable da'onai is attached to retains its
assignment and all other variables are cleared. *

This is a mistype. It should be {da'onai}


*4) da'oda'o means that all variables have their assignments cleared.*

This contradicts with how UI work. This can no longer be UI or UI becomes
impractical from the viewpoint of parsers.

